# The two most dangerous directories require explicit review.
#
# This file documents ownership. It only *blocks* a merge if the branch ruleset
# also turns on "Require review from Code Owners" — deliberately left off, since
# GitHub forbids approving your own pull request and a single-author repository
# would then be unable to merge its own infrastructure changes at all.
#
# The real gate on infrastructure is the required reviewer on the
# infra-*-apply GitHub Environments, which a run's own author *can* approve.
/infra/     @nlinhvu
/.github/   @nlinhvu
